  "snippet": "Episode 47 of the ongoing Halemaʻumaʻu eruption ended abruptly at 12:27 AM HST on May 15 after 9 hours of continuous lava fountaining from the north vent. Peak instantaneous effusion rate 360-390 yd³/s (275-300 m³/s) around 5 PM HST, average 270 yd³/s (220 m³/s). Fine ash and Pele's hair fell outside HVNP. Alert dropped WATCH→ADVISORY, Aviation ORANGE→YELLOW.",
